{{- /* Single source of truth for "can we read from Proton Pass right now?".
       Renders the literal string "true" or "false", same convention as
       is-container and is-devpod-platform.

       Two conditions, in this order and for different reasons:

       lookPath returns "" rather than failing when the binary is absent, which
       is the container case: .chezmoiexternals/pass-cli.toml is host-only, so
       inside a devpod container there is no pass-cli at all. It is also the
       first-apply case on a fresh machine, where the external has not landed
       yet.

       `pass-cli info` is the session test. It has to be wrapped in `sh -c ...
       && echo true || echo false` because chezmoi's `output` aborts the whole
       template on a non-zero exit — which is the very failure this gate exists
       to prevent. Wrapped, sh always exits 0 and the template gets a string.

       Cost is one pass-cli subprocess per apply that reaches this template,
       ~11ms unauthenticated. A stat on a session file would be cheaper but
       pass-cli documents no stable path for one. */ -}}
{{- if lookPath "pass-cli" -}}
{{- output "sh" "-c" "pass-cli info >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo true || echo false" | trim -}}
{{- else -}}false{{- end -}}
